# Secret handling

Never hardcode API keys, tokens, passwords, or private keys in source, config, rules, skills, fixtures, or commits.

Use the project's established secret mechanism (environment variables, secret manager, CI secrets). Locate it; do not invent vault APIs.

Do not read real `.env`, `credentials.*`, SSH private keys, or `.aws/credentials`. Templates named `*.example`, `*.sample`, or `*.template` are fine.

If a secret may already be exposed, tell the user. Do not echo secrets in chat or logs. Use clearly marked non-production placeholders in examples.
